/-
# §40.  A sharp *translated* window count for the ζ zeros

§38 gave the crude unit-window upper count `N(τ,τ+1] ≤ A_ζ·log(|τ|+3)` and §39 the dyadic
lower count.  Neither is sharp: the crude constant `A_ζ ≥ 1` is about `2π` times the true
local density `log(τ/2π)/(2π)`, and the dyadic statement only sees windows that contain a
whole dyadic block.  What the near-core lane actually needs is a *translated* window count
with the true density, which is what this module builds.

The `Zeta23` package proves all the ingredients for an arbitrary window, not just a dyadic
one; the dyadic shape of `rvM_main` comes only from the shape of its μ-integral input.
Assembled directly:

* `Zeta23.RvM.N_eq_halfContour_completedZeta` — the folded argument principle, for **any**
  pair of good heights `1 ≤ T₁ < T₂`;
* `Zeta23.RvM.halfContour_completedZeta_split` — `Λ = ζ · Γℝ` on the contour;
* `Zeta23.RvM.gamma_side` — the Γ half-contour is *exactly* `∫_{T₁}^{T₂} μ`, for any
  positive `T₁, T₂`;
* `Zeta23.RvM.backlund_horizontal` and `Zeta23.RvM.vertical_two` — the ζ half-contour is
  `O(log T₁ + log T₂)`;
* `Zeta23.RvM.exists_goodHeight` and `Zeta23.RvM.zeta_local_zero_count` — moving to good
  heights costs `O(log)`.

This yields `zeta_window_count_approx`:

    | N(a,b] − ∫_a^b μ |  ≤  C_w · log b      for all  T_w ≤ a ≤ b,

with `μ` the Γ-phase density, `μ(τ) ≈ log(τ/2π)/(2π)`.  Since `μ` is monotone
(`Zeta23.MuFields.mu_monotoneOn`), this gives sharp two-sided counts for *every* window,
`zeta_window_count_le` and `zeta_window_count_ge`.

Applied to the near-core gap split this removes both density hypotheses at once and with
the true constants: `zeta_gap_split_sharp_cutoff_bound` shows that gap-split positivity
forces

    (4/π²)·(J−1−D)·μ(t+D)  <  (2D+1)·μ(t+D) + 2·C_w·log(t+J) ,

i.e. an unconditional cutoff cap in which the two densities are literally the same number
`μ(t+D)` — the matched-constant situation that §37 could only assume.

Nothing here asserts or assumes the Riemann Hypothesis, and nothing weakens
`RiemannHypothesisFor`.  No `sorry`, no `axiom`, no Boolean receipt, no numerical
evidence, and no unproved imported authority or authority receipt: every imported input is
a checked Lean theorem of the `Zeta23` package, built from source in this checkout.
-/
import Zeta23Bridge.NearCoreZetaDyadicLongWindow
import Zeta23.RvM.Backlund
import Zeta23.RvM.GammaSide
import Zeta23.RvM.LocalCount
import Zeta23.GammaFacts.Mu

noncomputable section

open scoped Real
open Zeta23 MeasureTheory Complex

namespace Zeta23Bridge
namespace NearCoreZetaWindowCount

open Zeta23Bridge.LiteralWeilParityBalance
open Zeta23Bridge.LiteralWeilSameOrdinateEvenCone
open Zeta23Bridge.LiteralWeilOtherZerosChannel
open Zeta23Bridge.ReflectionPairCurvatureBound
open Zeta23Bridge.NearCoreDeterminantTaper
open Zeta23Bridge.NearCoreGapSplitEvaluation
open Zeta23Bridge.NearCoreGapSplitOptimization
